{"id":"code-parse-duration","title":"Strict duration parser","category":"code","difficulty":3,"prompt":"Write a Python function `parse_duration(text: str) -> int` that converts a duration such as \"1h30m\" into a number of seconds.\n\n- Units are d (days), h (hours), m (minutes) and s (seconds).\n- Each part is a non-negative integer followed by its unit, with no spaces.\n- Units must appear in the order d, h, m, s. Each unit may appear at most once, and at least one part is required.\n- Anything else raises ValueError.\n\nExamples: \"45s\" is 45, \"1h30m\" is 5400, \"1d2h3m4s\" is 93784.","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"parse_duration","tests":["assert parse_duration(\"45s\") == 45","assert parse_duration(\"2m\") == 120","assert parse_duration(\"1h30m\") == 5400","assert parse_duration(\"1d2h3m4s\") == 93784","assert parse_duration(\"0s\") == 0","assert parse_duration(\"10m5s\") == 605","assert raises(ValueError, parse_duration, \"\")","assert raises(ValueError, parse_duration, \"5\")","assert raises(ValueError, parse_duration, \"1m1h\")","assert raises(ValueError, parse_duration, \"1h1h\")","assert raises(ValueError, parse_duration, \"1.5h\")","assert raises(ValueError, parse_duration, \"1h 30m\")","assert raises(ValueError, parse_duration, \"-1h\")","assert raises(ValueError, parse_duration, \"90x\")"]},"reference":"```python\nimport re\n\n_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"(?:(\\d+)d)?(?:(\\d+)h)?(?:(\\d+)m)?(?:(\\d+)s)?\")\n\ndef parse_duration(text: str) -> int:\n    match = _PATTERN.fullmatch(text)\n    if not text or match is None or not any(match.groups()):\n        raise ValueError(f\"invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n    days, hours, minutes, seconds = (int(part) if part else 0 for part in match.groups())\n    return ((days * 24 + hours) * 60 + minutes) * 60 + seconds\n```","answers":["```python\nimport re\n\ndef parse_duration(text: str) -> int:\n    units = {\"d\": 86400, \"h\": 3600, \"m\": 60, \"s\": 1}\n    parts = re.findall(r\"(\\d+)([dhms])\", text)\n    if not parts:\n        raise ValueError(\"invalid duration\")\n    return sum(int(number) * units[unit] for number, unit in parts)\n```","```python\nimport re\n\n_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"(?:(\\d+)d)?(?:(\\d+)h)?(?:(\\d+)m)?(?:(\\d+)s)?\")\n\ndef parse_duration(text: str) -> int:\n    match = _PATTERN.fullmatch(text)\n    if not text or match is None or not any(match.groups()):\n        raise ValueError(f\"invalid duration: {text!r}\")\n    days, hours, minutes, seconds = (int(part) if part else 0 for part in match.groups())\n    return ((days * 24 + hours) * 60 + minutes) * 60 + seconds\n```"],"cells":[{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":0,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.64285714,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":9,"total":14,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.498,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":216,"output_tokens":257,"cost_usd":0.0001501,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":1,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.64285714,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":9,"total":14,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.498,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":216,"output_tokens":338,"cost